# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 009
# Act: SEG−  (Segment aimed at Ground)   Stance: Clearing   Site: Field
#
# The Structure triad's first operator, first use. Opens from :turn-7, NOT
# from :gap-008 — a refused attempt produces no closing register (no
# aperture, no perturbation choice), so there is nothing for a later turn
# to inherit from it. gap-008 is recorded, on the timeline, honestly; it
# does not advance the clock. Only earned turns do.
#
# Resolving the fork KERNEL.md left open: SEG becomes reachable without
# INS* closing first. SEG's precondition is an entity to draw a boundary
# around or within (EO Event Streaming §3, Operator Definitions: SEG
# "corresponds to WHERE, GROUP BY, FILTER, PARTITION") — that is satisfied
# by turn-7's anchor alone. INS*'s precondition — a second anchored entity
# to compose — is a different, harder requirement that SEG does not share.
# The Helix ordering (NUL→SIG→INS→SEG→...) orders OPERATORS, not every
# use of every operator; nothing in it says INS must close all three uses
# before SEG can open its first.
#
# SEG− itself: clearing the ground for a partition — establishing that a
# FIELD (a collection admitting boundaries) exists at all, before any
# specific boundary is drawn. The field here is the three committed series
# together (kernel/data/signal-a.json, signal-b.json, noise-control.json)
# — already read as a collection informally since turn-2; this turn is
# the first act that names it as one on purpose.
#
# Earning argument: precondition is turn-7 (an anchored entity belonging
# to the field). Refuted if no boundary within this field could ever be
# drawn without contradiction — checked next, at SEG+, not assumed here.

:turn-9  eot:opens        :turn-7 .
:turn-9  eot:act          eot:SEG- .
:turn-9  eot:stance       "Clearing" .
:turn-9  eot:site         "Field" .
:turn-9  eot:field        [ eot:members "kernel/data/signal-a.json, kernel/data/signal-b.json, kernel/data/noise-control.json" ] .
:turn-9  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
